my parents Tom and Judy met in college  got married at age 23 and have been  together ever since  so I guess I thought that's how the  formula worked you find someone young  plug in that unknown variable as X and  out spits Y happily ever after so given  that I just turned 30 this month I  thought I'd have it all figured out by  now I come home for the holidays and I  have one brother  Yates that's married with two kids and  another brother Pierce that's married  with two kids and six weddings scheduled  for this year and I'm feeling a small  amount of panic mounting or  claustrophobia like the walls of my  youth or uterus are closing in on me now  this isn't a pity party I'm a smart  successful woman I'm sophisticated yet  scrappy when I need to be I'm  well-connected but don't take myself too  seriously and I'm by no means trying to  sell myself here the truth is I've been  dating ever since the fifth grade why  haven't I figured this all out yet  I asked the person who knows me best  what my greatest weakness is and my mom  replied you live in denial that choices  must be made and she's right but  choosing a life partner it's a pretty  daunting choice  I mean maybe Cinderella only married  Prince Charming because she didn't meet  Prince Eric first look at that stud  muffin I decided to dive into the  research and I stumbled upon the  Stanford marshmallow experiment in this  study if a kid can resist the smaller  prize one marshmallow he'll get a bigger  reward later two marshmallows all I'm  saying is I'm holding out for my two  marshmallows  here's how I break down my dating  prospects on the x-axis I measure  long-term viability which I call the  Penguins access because penguins made  for life is this guy good to bring home  to the parents total penguin on the  y-axis I made ho ho ho on the y-axis I  measure how excited I am about someone  so I call that the butterflies axis do I  get nervous every time I send and  receive a text definite butterflies so  as previewed I'm a teacher I want to  fill this graph with examples like US  presidents bottom right quadrant you'd  have someone whose high penguin below  butterflies danger I might be settling  Jimmy Carter  really nice guy but  in the top left quadrant you'd have  someone who's high butterflies below  penguin fun but maybe not marriage  material bottom left quadrant not a  penguin and no butterfly as well that's  just wasting my time but I couldn't  think of a US president who's both and I  realized am i being unrealistic if I  wait and wait for this elusive top right  quadrant - marshmallow kind of man I  needed some answers so I set up focus  groups filled with my single friends  and in these conversations I learned  that Stanford grad students think about  this question a lot  whereas I make graphs some of my friends  make spreadsheets one of my female  friends Becca made what she called a  life partner matrix where she breaks  down what she's looking for into three  categories  emotional intellectual and physical she  further broke down each piece of this  pie into four slices for example for the  emotional connection  does he love my shortcomings is he  reciprocally vulnerable do we argue  fairly and lovingly in these focus  groups my friends also shared just how  difficult their dating journeys have  been one of my gay friends on hell  shared how he was making out with a guy  at a club only to realize that guy while  kissing him still had his eyes open and  was looking over on his shoulder  checking out all the other guys in the  room another friend Marco even made a  consulting slide deck analyzing his lack  of dating success on OkCupid  so  maybe I have nerdy friends may be  talking to Stanford grad student doesn't  accurately represent the population but  I realized my research was flawed if I  wanted to figure out how to choose a  life partner I needed to talk to my  friends in committed relationships so I  sent them a survey and asked one simple  question how did you choose your partner  here are three of my favorite responses  there was never a lightning bolt moment  per se just a gradual increase of  connection and affection a couple of  months in I realized I had something to  lose if we broke up we met on a road  trip and got stuck in horrendous traffic  and I remember it is the best drive of  my life I think I fell in love with him  that day I chose my partner by following  my heart and my gut I thought about how  to get her when we were single I thought  about how to keep her when we were  dating and now I think about how to make  her happy and build a life together now  that we are married isn't that something  in my research I talked to a guy named  Nate Bagley who traveled the country  interviewing married couples his  takeaway don't settle for mediocre love  epic love exists and he's seen it so I  reached out and asked if I could  interview him over Skype and in that  conversation  Nate Bagley said to me okay Jackie you  got five great guys in front of you  who's the right choice so I said the one  who inspires me to be my best self and  he said okay they all do that who's the  right choice  so I said the one who makes me laugh the  hardest and he said okay they're all  hilarious  who's the right choice so I said I come  home from a business trip who's the  first person I want to see and he said  okay you want to see all of them who's  the right choice and flustered  I said Nate I don't know how to choose  where is this going  he said to me Jackie  the right choice is the one you choose  and you make it right and if you're not  in a place to make that kind of  commitment you just might miss some  amazing candidates in January I was  dating a really nice guy coincidentally  named Nathan total penguin but after a  couple months I abandon ship I wasn't  prepared to commit so I ended it and  talking to Nate Bagley I realized I'm  the person at the club kissing with  their eyes open constantly looking over  someone's shoulder for what's better  so I said to Nate Bagley wait you said  don't settle for mediocre love epic love  exists that's what I'm waiting for  and he said Jackie epic love isn't this  innate thing epic love is the work you  both put in to make it better than  yesterday that's epic here I was so  afraid of settling for one marshmallow  and I realized there's a difference  between settling and settling in  settling in means loving someone for  their shortcomings closing your eyes  during the kiss and working every day at  being a better partner in this team the  takeaway here is choose who you love and  love who  choose writing this talk has changed  everything for me because after all the  research the focus groups the interviews  turns out all the work had to be done  here internally not externally the day  after I broke up with Nathan the penguin  he came over and he said to me I don't  accept your resignation and I thought  whoa that's pretty epic is this penguin  giving me butterflies so I withdrew my  resignation no I don't know if Nathan is  my two marshmallow man but I'm gonna  find out because this time I'm going  all-in  thank you
 

